From: h0cheung <hcheunh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: persist the current orientation when locking rotation

KWin keeps the sensor transform separate from the manual transform it saves.
When automatic rotation is disabled at an unchanged angle, sending only the
policy leaves the old manual transform in kwinoutputconfig.json. The current
session stays rotated, but the next login restores the old orientation.

Send the selected transform together with the policy when switching to Never.
This covers both Plasma Desktop and Plasma Mobile without a login script.

diff --git a/backends/kwayland/waylandoutputdevice.cpp b/backends/kwayland/waylandoutputdevice.cpp
index dc5b2d7..6d8c8b9 100644
--- a/backends/kwayland/waylandoutputdevice.cpp
+++ b/backends/kwayland/waylandoutputdevice.cpp
@@ -331,8 +331,13 @@ bool WaylandOutputDevice::setWlConfig(WaylandOutputManagement *management,
         wlConfig->scale(object(), wl_fixed_from_double(output->scale()));
     }
 
-    // rotation
-    if (toKScreenRotation(m_transform) != output->rotation()) {
+    // When locking rotation, persist the displayed orientation as the manual
+    // transform even if the sensor already rotated the output to that angle.
+    // Otherwise KWin restores an older manual orientation at the next login.
+    const bool lockingRotation = (output->capabilities() & Output::Capability::AutoRotation)
+        && m_autoRotatePolicy != static_cast<uint32_t>(Output::AutoRotatePolicy::Never)
+        && output->autoRotatePolicy() == Output::AutoRotatePolicy::Never;
+    if (toKScreenRotation(m_transform) != output->rotation() || lockingRotation) {
         changed = true;
         wlConfig->transform(object(), toKWaylandTransform(output->rotation()));
     }
